# Per-skill / per-CLI ownership (architecture.md §2b). In the GitHub-authority
# model, CODEOWNERS paths ARE the "who can approve what" mechanism — combined
# with branch protection (docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md) they replace a registry
# approval workflow. Edit these to your org's teams.

# Default owners for everything in the repo.
*                               @my-org/platform-team

# The convention contract and release wiring change the framework's behavior —
# guard them tightly.
/.skillrig-origin.toml          @my-org/platform-team
/release-please-config.json     @my-org/platform-team
/.goreleaser.yaml               @my-org/platform-team
/.github/                       @my-org/platform-team

# Backing CLIs — owned by the teams that maintain them.
/cmd/oxid/                      @my-org/platform-team

# Skills — own by domain. Add a line per skill or per skills/ subtree.
/skills/terraform-plan-review/  @my-org/platform-team

# External-source policy is a security decision.
/policy.toml                    @my-org/security
